**Issue:** Drop logic written as a loop with the wrong membership test and axis spelled out.
**Why:** `c in df` checks columns (ok here) but repeated full-frame drops each copy the frame; also drop(c) defaults to axis=0 (rows), so forgetting axis=1 deletes a row instead of a column.
**Fix:**
def keep(df, cols):
    return df.drop(columns=[c for c in cols if c in df.columns])

